1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ayzur of Abyssinia (720-775) was king of Abyssinia from 774 to 775, succeeding Oda Gosh of Abyssinia and preceding Rema Armah of Abyssinia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ayzur was the son of King Talatem of Abyssinia, and was a Miaphysite Christian of the Solomonic dynasty. Ayzur succeeded Oda Gosh of Abyssinia upon his death in 774 and reigned for one year as king of Abyssinia. When he died in 77
2 CONC 5, he was succeeded by Rema Armah of Abyssinia.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://historica.fandom.com/wiki/Ayzur_of_Abyssinia
