1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Letem of Abyssinia (679-741) was the king of Abyssinia from 725 to 741, succeeding Asgwomgum of Abyssinia and preceding Talatem of Abyssinia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Letem of Abyssinia was born in 679 to Asgwomgum of Abyssinia, and was a Miaphysite Christian from the Solomonic dynasty. Letem succeeded his father as king of Abyssinia when he died in 725, and he reigned until 741, when he died. 
2 CONC His son Talatem of Abyssinia succeeded him.
2 CONT
